module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Artin.ContractionLimitTowerRingMap
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Artin.ContractionLimitCompletionAlgebra
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.ProperGlobalSections.AdicCompletionSmall

/-!
# The tower ring of a proper algebraic space is the completion of its global functions

For a proper morphism `g : X ⟶ V` of algebraic spaces with `V` affine and locally Noetherian,
`A = Γ(V, 𝒪_V)`, `C = Γ(X, 𝒪_X)` and an ideal `I ⊆ A`, the theorem on formal functions in degree
zero (`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.adicCompletionFibreFunctionsEquiv`) identifies the `I`-adic
completion `C^∧` of the finite `A`-module `C` with the ring
`lim_n Γ(X ×_V Spec (A / I^{n+1}), 𝒪)` of `AlgebraicGeometry.Artin.FormalRing.towerRing`. Under
this identification `α : A^∧ ⟶ lim_n Γ(X ×_V Spec (A / I^{n+1}), 𝒪)` is the completion of
`A ⟶ C`, and the restriction to the fibres is the map `C ⟶ C^∧`.

When the kernel and the cokernel of `A ⟶ C` are killed by a power of `I` (in the proof of
Stacks 0GI5: `X = V'_μ` proper over `V_μ` and an isomorphism away from `Z_μ`), this transports
the commutative algebra of `AlgebraicGeometry.Artin.ContractionLimitCompletionAlgebra` ("these
modules are equal to their completions") to `α`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Artin.FormalRing.towerComparison`: the bijection
  `C^∧ ⟶ lim_n Γ(X ×_V Spec (A / I^{n+1}), 𝒪)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Artin.FormalRing.towerComparison_of`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Artin.FormalRing.towerComparison_map`: the comparison carries `C ⟶ C^∧` to
  the restriction to the fibres and the completion of `A ⟶ C` to `α`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Artin.FormalRing.exists_eq_alpha_add_towerOf`,
  `exists_pullbackRingHom_eq_of_towerOf_eq_alpha`, `exists_algebraMap_eq_of_alpha_eq_zero`,
  `exists_alpha_eq_of_mem_towerFiltration`, `exists_eq_zero_of_alpha_eq_zero_of_mem`: the
  tower ring is generated by the images of `A^∧` and `C`, an element of `C` whose image comes
  from `A^∧` comes from `A`, the kernel of `α` is the image of the kernel of `A ⟶ C`, the
  Artin–Rees lemma for `α`, and the kernel of `α` meets a power of `I A^∧` in zero.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GI5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GI5)
-/

